# MODEL RULES – SmartCartPro

## 1. Entities are DB-only
- Classes in SmartCartPro.Entities (Company, Store, License, AuditLog …) are used ONLY inside Repositories (EF/DB mapping).
- NEVER return, accept or expose an Entity from a Repository interface, Service, Controller or View.
- No "Dto" suffix classes. Remove/replace existing *Dto classes.

## 2. Three model types per operation – exact naming
| Purpose | Name format | Example | Used between |
|---|---|---|---|
| View / form model (Razor + validation) | In{Entity}{Action}View | InStoreUpdateView | View ⇄ Controller |
| Input passed down | Input{Entity}{Action} | InputStoreUpdate | Controller → Service → Repository interface |
| Output returned up | Output{Entity}{Action} | OutputStoreUpdate | Repository → Service → Controller |

Actions: Create, Update, Select (single), List, Delete, Upsert.

## 3. Where each model lives
- One file per module under Models/: CompanyModels.cs, StoreModels.cs, LicenseModels.cs, …
- Namespace: SmartCartPro.Models.
- One #region per operation; region holds In…View / Input… / Output… that exist.
- DataAnnotations ONLY on In…View. Input… and Output… stay plain (Output may have ResponseCode, ResponseMsg, StatusCode).

## 4. Mapping (controller owns View → Input)
- Controller: map InXxxView → InputXxx with an **explicit named variable**, then call the service in a **separate** statement.
- Do **not** use `InputXxx.From(view)`, mapping helpers on Input models, AutoMapper, or pass `new InputXxx { … }` inline into the service call.
- Repository: InputXxx → Entity and Entity → OutputXxx only inside the repository (prefer Select projection).

```csharp
// ✅ GOOD
var input = new InputCategoryUpdate
{
    IdCategory = model.IdCategory,
    CategoryName = model.CategoryName,
    // …
};
var result = await _svc.UpdateCategoryAsync(input, ct);

// ❌ BAD
var result = await _svc.UpdateCategoryAsync(InputCategoryUpdate.From(model), ct);
var result = await _svc.UpdateCategoryAsync(new InputCategoryUpdate { … }, ct);
```

## 5. Interface signatures (pattern)
Task<OutputStoreSelect?> GetStoreAsync(InputStoreSelect input, CancellationToken ct = default);
Task<OutputStoreList> ListStoresAsync(InputStoreList input, CancellationToken ct = default);
Task<OutputStoreCreate> CreateStoreAsync(InputStoreCreate input, CancellationToken ct = default);
Task<OutputStoreUpdate> UpdateStoreAsync(InputStoreUpdate input, CancellationToken ct = default);

## 6. Do not
- Do not put [Required]/[MaxLength] on Input/Output classes.
- Do not reuse one model for both input and output.
- Do not add a model that is not used.

## 7. Validation – In…View only (PerSuitePlus style)
- Validation attributes ONLY on In{Entity}{Action}View. Input/Output stay plain.
- Every property gets `[Display(Name = "…")]`.
- Prefer `SmartCartPro.CustomModelValidation` attributes over built-in alone:
  - Required text: `[Required]` + `[StringLengthValidation]` + `[NoScriptTags]`
  - Optional text: `[StringLengthValidation(0,max)]` + `[NoScriptTags]`
  - Name: `[TrimmedString]` or `[DisallowCharacters]` + `[NoScriptTags]`
  - Required dropdown id: `[Required]` + `[GreaterThanZero(ErrorMessage="Something went wrong/…")]`
  - Optional dropdown id: `[GreaterThanOrEqualToZero]`
  - Phone optional: `[PhoneIfNotEmpty]` + `[PhoneNumber]`
  - Email optional: `[EmailIfNotEmpty]` + `[MatchRegexAllowNull]`
  - Zip / Lat / Long: `[ZipCode]` / `[ValidLatitude]` / `[ValidLongitude]`
  - Date range: `[DateGreaterThanOrEqualTo("FromProperty")]` on To field
  - Fixed values: `[AllowedValues]` (built-in) or `[EnumDefined]` for int enums
- User fields → plain messages. Hidden/system fields (ids, codes, mode) → prefix `"Something went wrong/"`.
